  "id": "Compound::DB00549 - Gene::5742",
  "verbalization": "Zafirlukast, a member of the leukotriene receptor antagonists class, exhibits a consistent relationship with Ptgs1, the prostanoid receptor. The evidence suggests that Zafirlukast binds to Ptgs1, as indicated by multiple paths linking it to this receptor. This binding is supported by the shared lowest common ancestor (LCA) of Zafirlukast and Montelukast, both of which are classified under the organonitrogen heterocyclic compound category and as anti-asthmatic agents. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores reinforces the biological relevance of this interaction.\n\nThe evidence also highlights that Zafirlukast is associated with vasculitic rash and allergic granulomatous angiitis, conditions that are linked to Montelukast and, consequently, Ptgs1. These findings suggest that Zafirlukast may modulate inflammatory pathways involving Ptgs1, potentially through the inhibition of leukotriene signaling. However, the specific mechanism by which Zafirlukast influences Ptgs1 remains to be fully elucidated, and further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction and functional role in disease pathogenesis.",
